BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (  # The Tale of the Spring and the River) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (  In the beginning, there lived a Spring at the mountain's peak and a River in the valley below.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (     Each day, the Sun blessed the Spring with five drops of liquid silver.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (  The Spring faced a choice: hold the silver close, or release it down the mountain. The Spring ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (    knew a secret-any silver that flowed downward would triple as it tumbled through the magical) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (     stones.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (  One day, the Spring decided to trust. It released its silver, watching it multiply into fiftee) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (    n drops as it reached the River below. The River, now abundant, faced its own choice: keep a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (    ll the silver, or send some back up the mountain.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (  The River remembered the Spring's generosity. It knew the Spring had sacrificed, had trusted. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (    So the River returned half its treasure, sending back seven drops that climbed upward like s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (    ilver salmon.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (  And so they prospered. The Spring ended with more than it began, the River flourished with its) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (     share, and both learned the ancient truth: that wealth shared grows larger, that trust retu) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (    rned builds fountains, and that the path to abundance flows both ways.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
