BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (      The Spring faced a choice: hold the silver close, or release it down the mountain. The Spr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (        ing knew a secret-any silver that flowed downward would triple as it tumbled through the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (         magical stones.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (      One day, the Spring decided to trust. It released its silver, watching it multiply into fi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (        fteen drops as it reached the River below. The River, now abundant, faced its own choice) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (        : keep all the silver, or send some back up the mountain.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (      The River remembered the Spring's generosity. It knew the Spring had sacrificed, had trust) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (        ed. So the River returned half its treasure, sending back seven drops that climbed upwar) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (        d like silver salmon.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (      And so they prospered. The Spring ended with more than it began, the River flourished with) Tj ET
